    "updated_at": "2021-08-31T11:55:03Z",
    "body": "Looks like Chrome and Safari (at least desktop) don't sniff it indeed [0], curiously. It's however mandatory to implement `HTMLMediaElement` (the Content-Type is to be ignored), so there should be steps to sniff here.\r\n\r\n[0]: I tested serving a HLS playlist file with `application/octet-stream` and no extension as the `src` attribute of an `HTMLMediaElement`, and seeing what implementations do. Firefox plays it, Safari and Chrome don't.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/comments/909166569/reactions",
